<blockquote>
<p>It is worth mentioning that all the volcanoes on on Io are in fact Cryovolcanoes&#8230;.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Unless <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volcanism_on_Io">Wikipedia</a> is outright lying, the volcanoes on Io are <strong>not</strong> cryovolcanoes, but &quot;regular&quot; hot volcanoes spewing either basalt, sulfur, or ultramafic silicates. Io's heat comes from tidal forces due to its proximity to Jupiter and the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orbital_resonance#Mean_motion_resonances_in_the_Solar_System">effects</a> of Europa and Ganymede on Io's orbit. To be sure, most of the volcanic objects in the outer Solar System are cryovolcanic, but Io is the exception because of its unique situation.</p>

